            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sarah Jo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used this recipe for honey-dijon chicken. I used reduced fat mayonnaise and because I was using homemade italian seasoning in the coating for the chicken, I used white wine vinegar in this recipe. (I wasn't really sure that rice wine vinegar would go well with italian seasoning, to be honest). It was absolutely perfect--just enough to coat four halved chicken breasts and it made the chicken wonderful. My husband and kids inhaled the chicken dish. I'll use this recipe again and again."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "7.19.17 Enjoyed this today as a dipping sauce for some corned beef hash croquettes. For our personal tastes, I cut the honey in half and doubled the hot sauce. I can see this sauce being a perfect match for so many things, and I love how easy it is to mix up. This one’s a keeper!",
            "datePublished": "2017-07-19T16:37:47.677Z"
          },
